# Line endings are DISABLED repo-wide, deliberately.
#
# `protocol/instrument-snapshot/` records a SHA256 for each of its 13 modules + 2 configs
# (see PIN.json), and `src/instrument/run_pinned_sidecar.py` re-hashes them and REFUSES TO
# LAUNCH on a mismatch. Git's default `core.autocrlf` on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout, which changes every byte of every hashed file and would silently break the
# pinned instrument for anyone who clones this repository -- the launcher would fail, and
# `instrument_hashes()` would report drift on a clean checkout.
#
# A research artifact whose whole thesis is "verify, do not trust" cannot ship a checkout
# path that falsifies its own hashes. So: no conversion anywhere.
* -text

# Binary-ish artefacts, stated explicitly for clarity even though `* -text` covers them.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.gz   binary
*.zip  binary
*.csv  -text
*.json -text

# Linguist: this is a research artifact, not a library.
paper/MANUSCRIPT.md   linguist-generated=true
paper/MANUSCRIPT.md   linguist-documentation
results/*.json        linguist-generated=true
protocol/instrument-snapshot/** linguist-vendored
